### 1. Register a new user
# @name register
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Farah Yusni",
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 2. Duplicate register -> expect 409
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Farah Yusni",
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 3. Invalid input -> expect 400
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "bad-email",
  "password": "123"
}

###

### 4. Login -> expect 200 + token
# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "abc12345"
}

###

### 5. Wrong password -> expect 401
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "farah@gmail.com",
  "password": "wrongpass"
}

###

### 6. Protected route, no token -> expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ping

###

### 7. Protected route, with token -> expect 404 (no route, but auth passed)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/ping
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}